            <div xml:id="d1278">

                <pb facs="0510" n="2212" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p2/pg2212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.74/2–954: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1278<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-02-09T12:00:00+01:00">February 9,
                        1954—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dulte 55. Limit distribution. For President,
                    copy for Acting Secretary. From Secretary. Eden giving considerable concern here to Egyptian problem. Says
                    question of whether to try to settle with Egyptians will be dealt with Wednesday
                    Cabinet meeting. He is strongly urging that conditions are ripe now for
                    settlement, and he hopes Cabinet will go along, although he admits Winston very difficult.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"><hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Dulles</hi></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
